    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "root = [10, 5, 15, 3, 7, null, 18], low = 7, high = 15             ->  32\nroot = [10, 5, 15, 3, 7, 13, 18, 1, null, 6], low = 6, high = 10   ->  23   (6 + 7 + 10)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: prune what can't be in range"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Summing every node works for any tree. A BST lets you skip whole subtrees: if a node is **below `low`**, everything on its left is smaller still — only its **right** side can contain values in range. If it's **above `high`**, only its **left** side can. Only nodes inside the range need both sides searched."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Visit every node"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function rangeSumBST(node, low, high) {\n  if (node === null) return 0;\n  const self = node.val >= low && node.val <= high ? node.val : 0;\n  return self + rangeSumBST(node.left, low, high) + rangeSumBST(node.right, low, high);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def range_sum_bst(node, low, high):\n    if node is None:\n        return 0\n    own = node.val if low <= node.val <= high else 0\n    return own + range_sum_bst(node.left, low, high) + range_sum_bst(node.right, low, high)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int rangeSumBST(TreeNode node, int low, int high) {\n    if (node == null) return 0;\n    int self = node.val >= low && node.val <= high ? node.val : 0;\n    return self + rangeSumBST(node.left, low, high) + rangeSumBST(node.right, low, high);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int rangeSumBST(TreeNode* node, int low, int high) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return 0;\n    int self = node->val >= low && node->val <= high ? node->val : 0;\n    return self + rangeSumBST(node->left, low, high) + rangeSumBST(node->right, low, high);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(h).** Ignores the ordering."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Prune by the BST ordering"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "range-sum-bst",
      "caption": "Too small: only the right side can help. Too big: only the left. In range: add it and search both sides."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function rangeSumBST(node, low, high) {\n  if (node === null) return 0;\n  if (node.val < low) return rangeSumBST(node.right, low, high);    // node and its left side are too small\n  if (node.val > high) return rangeSumBST(node.left, low, high);    // node and its right side are too big\n  return node.val + rangeSumBST(node.left, low, high) + rangeSumBST(node.right, low, high);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def range_sum_bst(node, low, high):\n    if node is None:\n        return 0\n    if node.val < low:\n        return range_sum_bst(node.right, low, high)    # node and its left side are too small\n    if node.val > high:\n        return range_sum_bst(node.left, low, high)     # node and its right side are too big\n    return node.val + range_sum_bst(node.left, low, high) + range_sum_bst(node.right, low, high)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int rangeSumBST(TreeNode node, int low, int high) {\n    if (node == null) return 0;\n    if (node.val < low) return rangeSumBST(node.right, low, high);   // node and its left side are too small\n    if (node.val > high) return rangeSumBST(node.left, low, high);   // node and its right side are too big\n    return node.val + rangeSumBST(node.left, low, high) + rangeSumBST(node.right, low, high);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int rangeSumBST(TreeNode* node, int low, int high) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return 0;\n    if (node->val < low) return rangeSumBST(node->right, low, high);   // node and its left side are too small\n    if (node->val > high) return rangeSumBST(node->left, low, high);   // node and its right side are too big\n    return node->val + rangeSumBST(node->left, low, high) + rangeSumBST(node->right, low, high);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(h + k)** where k is the number of values in range — the walk only enters a subtree that can hold an answer. **Space O(h).** In the worst case (everything in range) it's still O(n), but a narrow range in a big balanced tree costs about O(log n)."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. The same pruning with a stack"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function rangeSumBST(root, low, high) {\n  let sum = 0;\n  const stack = [root];\n  while (stack.length > 0) {\n    const node = stack.pop();\n    if (node === null) continue;\n    if (node.val >= low && node.val <= high) sum += node.val;\n    if (node.val > low) stack.push(node.left);      // the left side may still hold values >= low\n    if (node.val < high) stack.push(node.right);    // the right side may still hold values <= high\n  }\n  return sum;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def range_sum_bst(root, low, high):\n    total = 0\n    stack = [root]\n    while stack:\n        node = stack.pop()\n        if node is None:\n            continue\n        if low <= node.val <= high:\n            total += node.val\n        if node.val > low:\n            stack.append(node.left)       # the left side may still hold values >= low\n        if node.val < high:\n            stack.append(node.right)      # the right side may still hold values <= high\n    return total"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int rangeSumBST(TreeNode root, int low, int high) {\n    int sum = 0;\n    Deque<TreeNode> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();\n    if (root != null) stack.push(root);\n    while (!stack.isEmpty()) {\n        TreeNode node = stack.pop();\n        if (node.val >= low && node.val <= high) sum += node.val;\n        if (node.val > low && node.left != null) stack.push(node.left);      // may still hold values >= low\n        if (node.val < high && node.right != null) stack.push(node.right);   // may still hold values <= high\n    }\n    return sum;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int rangeSumBST(TreeNode* root, int low, int high) {\n    int sum = 0;\n    vector<TreeNode*> stack = {root};\n    while (!stack.empty()) {\n        TreeNode* node = stack.back();\n        stack.pop_back();\n        if (node == nullptr) continue;\n        if (node->val >= low && node->val <= high) sum += node->val;\n        if (node->val > low) stack.push_back(node->left);      // the left side may still hold values >= low\n        if (node->val < high) stack.push_back(node->right);    // the right side may still hold values <= high\n    }\n    return sum;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(h + k), space O(h)** for the stack — the same work without recursion."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Visit every node",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "It checks **every node**, ignoring the ordering.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "Recursion **as deep as the tree**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Prune by the BST ordering",
          "time": "O(h + k)",
          "timeWhy": "It only enters subtrees that **can hold** values in range: one path down (h) plus the **k** values found.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "Recursion along the visited paths."
        },
        {
          "approach": "The same pruning with a stack",
          "time": "O(h + k)",
          "timeWhy": "The **same pruned walk**, without recursion.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "The stack holds the pending subtrees along the walk."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Nothing in range** — 0.",
        "**Everything in range** — every node is visited; no pruning helps.",
        "**low = high** — at most one value counts.",
        "**Range covers the root only** — both children may still need checking."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Count nodes in a range** — the same pruning, adding 1 instead of the value.",
        "**All values in a range, sorted** — an in-order walk with the same pruning.",
        "**Trim a BST** — keep only the nodes in range, re-linking the rest (Pattern 2)."
      ]
    }
